1:46:45 PM [express] POST /api/ai/chat 200 in 70862ms :: {"response":"Okay, I will provide you with a weight loss diet plan tailored specifically for you, considering your age, sex, blood type, height, weight, and lack of existing medical conditions. Remember that consistent effort and healthy lifestyle choices beyond just diet are crucial for successful weight management. Also note that these recommendations should always be discussed with your physician prior to implementation!\n\n## 🌅 Breakfast\n\n*   **Oats Porridge:** 1 cup cooked oatmeal made with milk(or almond milk if preferred), topped with chopped fruits like berries and a sprinkle of cinnamon. Approximately 350 Calories.\n*   **Boiled Egg White**: One boiled egg white provides approximately 17 kcal.\n\n## 🍎 Mid-Morning Snack\n\n*   **Apple Slices with Almond Butter:** A medium apple sliced into wedges served with 2 tablespoons of natural almond butter. Provides fiber, healthy fats, and sustained energy. About 200 Calories.\n\n## 🍽️ Lunch\n\n*   **Vegetable Upma:** Made from semolina (rava) tempered with mustard seeds, curry leaves, onions, green chilies, and mixed vegetables such as carrots, peas, beans etc. Served with a side salad of cucumber and tomato. Approx. 400 Calories.\n*   **Small portion of sprouts Salad.**\n\n## 🌆 Evening Snack\n\n*   **Roasted Chana Chaat:** Roasted chickpeas seasoned with spices like cumin, coriander, chaat masala, lemon juice, and finely chopped onion. Approximately 150 Calories.\n\n## 🌙 Dinner\n\n*   **Dal Makhani (small serving):** 1 cup of Dal Makhani prepared using minimal fat content. It can also include some sauteed Vegetables along with it. Approximate Calorie count = 300 Calories.\n*  **Roti :** Two whole wheat rotis.\n\n## ⚠️ Foods to Avoid\n\n*   Processed snacks (chips, cookies, pastries)\n*   Sugary drinks (colas, juices)\n*   Fried foods\n*   Excessive amounts of cheese and creamy sauces\n*   Refined carbohydrates (white bread, pasta)\n*   Large servings sizes overall.\n\n## 💡 Why This Plan\n\n*   **Weight Loss Focus:** The primary focus here is calorie reduction through mindful eating practices while ensuring nutrient adequacy. Portion control plays a vital role.\n*   **Balanced Macronutrients:** The plan includes complex carbs (oats, roti), lean protein sources (dal, chana, egg whites), and good quality fats (almond butter, olive oils used sparingly during cooking).\n*   **Fiber Rich Diet:** Emphasis on high-fiber options helps promote satiety, regulate digestion, and support gut health which aids in weight management. Fiber rich ingredients include Oats, Apple, Sprouts, Rava, Vegetable upma, and Rotis .\n*   **Hydration:** Drinking plenty of water throughout the day supports metabolism and reduces cravings. Aim for at least 8 glasses daily.\n* **Low Glycemic Index Food Choices:** Choosing lower GI carbohydrate source ensures stable blood sugar level preventing spikes after meals leading to better appetite regulation. Examples - Oatmeal, Whole Wheat Roti , Brown Rice instead of White Rice.\n\n[MACROS: Protein 35%, Carbs 40%, Fat 25%]","followUpQuestions":[]}























